[17592186147890 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9bc7c273-0dfe-58b5-98ac-f3b5aaeadbfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147890 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $25,$ and the percentage is $120%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n120%=120÷100=1.2\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =120%\\times 25 \\\\  & =1.2\\times 25 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $120%$ of $25$ is $30.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n120%=\\frac{120}{100}=\\frac{120÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =120%\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\times 25 \\\\  & =6\\times \\frac{25}{5} \\\\  & =6\\times 5 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $120%$ of $25$ is $30.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148370 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148370 #edb/ref 1061 54220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148370 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d3e65926-0f7c-5d3a-b5ff-962bec1f0e24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148370 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186148789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148371 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148371 #edb/ref 1061 54221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148371 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "092306a2-20ad-5d22-9e48-cb1c1ae8774d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148371 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148372 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148372 #edb/ref 1061 54224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148372 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0674771c-1511-5f16-a17e-54ff8d00c79e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148372 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148373 #edb/ref 1061 54227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148373 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c8e96f68-307a-58c2-8d26-9f11f68fde49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148373 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148789 #edb/ref 1064 "We can find a percentage part of a number using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part} = \\textrm{percentage} \\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nTo illustrate, let's calculate $16 \\%$ of $300.$\n\nHere, the whole is $300$ and the percentage is $16 \\% .$ So, the part is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part} = 16\\% \\times 300.\n$$\n\nBut how do we multiply a percentage by a number? We have two methods of doing this. Let's apply both and check that they give the same answer.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n16\\% = 16 \\div 100 = 0.16\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 300 \\\\  & =0.16\\times 300 \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $16\\%$ of $300$ is $48.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n16\\% = \\dfrac{16}{100}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 300 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{100}\\times 300 \\\\  & =16\\times \\frac{300}{100} \\\\  & =16\\times 3 \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $16 \\%$ of $300$ is $48.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148789 #edb/ref 1065 8198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148789 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "41c3207b-f9a6-5e36-9a0b-a6ad0c9e8a18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148789 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441624 #edb/ref 1080 "100" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441624 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441624 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11421dbe-1fb6-5