t{whole} \\\\  & =70%\\times 80 \\\\  & =0.7\\times 80 \\\\  & =56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $70%$ of $80$ is $56.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n70%=\\frac{70}{100}=\\frac{70÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{7}{10}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =70%\\times 80 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}\\times 80 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{80}{10} \\\\  & =7\\times 8 \\\\  & =56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $70%$ of $80$ is $56.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441673 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441673 #edb/ref 1069 "q-186026" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441673 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441673 #edb/ref 1071 "$225%$ of $32$ is equal to{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441673 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28285ccd-1dac-57e7-a3e5-0e93bbb0a6e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441673 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $32,$ and the percentage is $225%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n225%=225÷100=2.25\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =225%\\times 32 \\\\  & =2.25\\times 32 \\\\  & =72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $225%$ of $32$ is $72.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n225%=\\frac{225}{100}=\\frac{225÷25}{100÷25}=\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =225%\\times 32 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\times 32 \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{32}{4} \\\\  & =9\\times 8 \\\\  & =72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $225%$ of $32$ is $72.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441674 