}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1.5%$ of $60$ is $0.9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441684 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441684 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160842" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441684 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441684 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $115%$ of $80?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441684 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e7f35be5-687e-57cd-bcc5-6295920b0ded" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441684 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $80,$ and the percentage is $115%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n115%=115÷100=1.15\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =115%\\times 80 \\\\  & =1.15\\times 80 \\\\  & =92\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $115%$ of $80$ is $92.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n115%=\\frac{115}{100}=\\frac{115÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{23}{20}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =115%\\times 80 \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{20}\\times 80 \\\\  & =23\\times \\frac{80}{20} \\\\  & =23\\times 4 \\\\  & =92\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $115%$ of $80$ is $92.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441685 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441685 #edb/ref 1069 "q-186013" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441685 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441685 #edb/ref 1071 "$16%$ of $75$ is equal to{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441685 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f69f8dbf-c5fe-511e-99d9-e38d8cf15603" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441685 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}